From a0e2e516d6d7d24ad610a40d900169de8ed3e256 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:52:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] MAINTAINERS: add the HiSilicon STB regulator entry

The PMOC voltage regulator driver has no maintainer entry. The driver is
a DT-binding driver of this platform, reviewed under linux-kernel.

Register the driver with its binding.

Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
---
 MAINTAINERS | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

--- a/MAINTAINERS
+++ b/MAINTAINERS
@@ -12196,6 +12196,13 @@ S:	Maintained
 F:	Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/hisilicon,hi6421-spmi-pmic.yaml
 F:	drivers/mfd/hi6421-spmi-pmic.c
 
+HISILICON STB VOLTAGE REGULATOR DRIVER
+M:	David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
+L:	linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org
+S:	Maintained
+F:	Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/hisilicon,hi3798cv200-regulator.yaml
+F:	drivers/regulator/histb-regulator.c
+
 HISILICON TRUE RANDOM NUMBER GENERATOR V2 SUPPORT
 M:	Weili Qian <qianweili@huawei.com>
 S:	Maintained
